David Chmelik posted:
>How can I keep him alive down there?

I found taking pets into Gehennom to not be worth the bother. The maps
being entirely mazes of one-unit-wide corridors means pets tend to get
away from you and die stupidly while you're not around to take care of
them. In fact it's more likely that they'll get turned into something
useless because the narrow corridor means there's no way they can avoid
flying onto a polymorph trap. To put it another way you wouldn't go in
there without magic resistance so neither should they.

If you really have a pet you want to keep alive I would advise locking
it in one of the rooms in the Castle and re-taming it on the way back
up.

